{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-136379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves from the origin with a constant velocity of  $(2i+5j)\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $3$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=2i+5j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(2i+5j)(3) \\\\  & =(6i+15j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-136379" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136379" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-i+2j)\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "(5i+8j)\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "(6i+15j)\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "-3i\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "3j\\,\\text{cm}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136379" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(6i+15j)\\,\\text{cm}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(i-4j)\\,\\text{km}$ with a constant velocity of $i\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $2$ hours." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=i-4j,\\,u=i.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=2\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(i-4j)+i(2) \\\\  & =(i-4j)+2i \\\\  & =(3i-4j)\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-136375" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136375" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(2i+4j)\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "(3i-4j)\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "(i-8j)\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "2i\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "2j\\,\\text{km}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136375" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(3i-4j)\\,\\text{km}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with a constant velocity of $(6i+2j)\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ If its initial position is ${r}_{0}=(3i-5j)\\,\\text{cm},$ find its position vector $r$ after $5$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}  \n$i\\,\\,+$  \n{{field-2}}  \n$j)\\text{cm}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When a particle (or object) moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector at time $t$ is given by the equation\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position vector.\n\nIn this case,\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=3i-5j,\\,u=6i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=5\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(3i-5j)+(6i+2j)(5) \\\\  & =3i-5j+30i+10j \\\\  & =(\\,33\\,i+5\\,j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-280488" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280488" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "33"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280488" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280488" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A bird glides with a constant velocity of $(-2i-1j)\\,\\text{yd/s}.$ If it starts at the position ${r}_{0}=(6i+4j)\\,\\text{yd},$ find its position vector $r$ after $3$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}  \n$i\\,\\,+$  \n{{field-2}}  \n$j)\\text{yd}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When a particle (or object) moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector at time $t$ is given by the equation\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position vector.\n\nIn this case,\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=6i+4j,\\,u=-2i-1j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the bird after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(6i+4j)+(-2i-1j)(3) \\\\  & =6i+4j-6i-3j \\\\  & =(\\,0\\,i+1\\,j)\\,\\text{yd}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-280491" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280491" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280491" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280491" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An autonomous submarine travels with a constant velocity of $(3i+5j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$ If its initial position is ${r}_{0}=(-3i+0j)\\,\\text{km},$ find the position vector $r$ after $3$ hours.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}  \n$i\\,\\,+$  \n{{field-2}}  \n$j)\\text{km}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When a particle (or object) moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector at time $t$ is given by the equation\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position vector.\n\nIn this case,\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-3i+0j,\\,u=3i+5j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the submarine after $t=3\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(-3i+0j)+(3i+5j)(3) \\\\  & =-3i+0j+9i+15j \\\\  & =(\\,6\\,i+15\\,j)\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-280492" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280492" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280492" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280492" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A skier begins at the position ${r}_{0}=(-3i+2j)\\,\\text{m}$ with an initial velocity of $(5i-2j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and accelerates at $(2i+j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Determine the position vector after $2$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-3i+2j,\\,u=5i-2j,\\,a=2i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the skier after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(-3i+2j)+(5i-2j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(2i+j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(-3i+2j)+(5i-2j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(8i+4j) \\\\  & =(-3i+2j)+(10i-4j)+(4i+2j) \\\\  & =(\\,11\\,i+0\\,j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-280513" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280513" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280513" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280513" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $-2j\\,\\text{ft}$ with an acceleration of $4i\\,{\\text{ft/min}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(3i+j)\\,\\text{ft/min}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $2$ minutes." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-2j,\\,u=3i+j,\\,a=4i.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=2\\,\\text{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(-2j)+(3i+j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(4i)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =-2j+(6i+2j)+2(4i) \\\\  & =6i+8i \\\\  & =14i\\,\\text{ft}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-136416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-7i-14j)\\,\\text{ft}"] ["math" "(15i+5j)\\,\\text{ft}"] ["math" "(5i-j)\\,\\text{ft}"] ["math" "-7j\\,\\text{ft}"] ["math" "14i\\,\\text{ft}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14i\\,\\text{ft}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves from the origin with an initial velocity of $(6i+8j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and experiences a constant acceleration of $(-2i-10j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Determine the position vector of the ball after $1$ second.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=6i+8j,\\,a=-2i-10j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=1\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(6i+8j)(1)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i-10j)(1)^{2} \\\\  & =(6i+8j)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i-10j) \\\\  & =(6i+8j)+(-1i-5j) \\\\  & =(\\,5\\,i+3\\,j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-280504" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280504" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280504" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280504" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A toy rocket is launched from the origin with an initial velocity of $(2i+6j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and a constant acceleration of $(i+5j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Determine the position vector of the rocket after $2$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=2i+6j,\\,a=i+5j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the rocket after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(2i+6j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+5j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(4i+12j)+2(i+5j) \\\\  & =(4i+12j)+(2i+10j) \\\\  & =(\\,6\\,i+22\\,j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-280507" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280507" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280507" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280507" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "22"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(-i+j)\\,\\text{mm}$ with an acceleration of $(2i-6j)\\,{\\text{mm/min}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(-3i+2j)\\,\\text{mm/min}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $5$ minutes." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-i+j,\\,u=-3i+2j,\\,a=2i-6j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=5\\,\\text{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(-i+j)+(-3i+2j)(5)+\\frac{1}{2}(2i-6j)(5)^{2} \\\\  & =(-i+j)+(-15i+10j)+25(i-3j) \\\\  & =(-16i+11j)+(25i-75j) \\\\  & =(9i-64j)\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(16i+49j)\\,\\text{mm}"] ["math" "(25i+36j)\\,\\text{mm}"] ["math" "(3i-8j)\\,\\text{mm}"] ["math" "(4i-7j)\\,\\text{mm}"] ["math" "(9i-64j)\\,\\text{mm}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(9i-64j)\\,\\text{mm}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A mail truck departs from the post office at the origin and drives with a constant velocity of $(4i-3j)\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ Determine the distance $(|r|)$ from the truck to the origin after $2$ hours.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mi}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=4i-3j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the truck after $t=2\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(4i-3j)(2) \\\\  & =(8i-6j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the truck to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|8i-6j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-280526" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280526" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A car accelerates from rest at the origin with an acceleration of $(3i-4j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $2i\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the distance from the car to the origin$(|r|)$ after $4$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=2i,\\,a=3i-4j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the car after $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(2i)(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(3i-4j)(4)^{2} \\\\  & =8i+8(3i-4j) \\\\  & =8i+24i-32j \\\\  & =(32i-32j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the car to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|32i-32j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(32)^{2}+(-32)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1024+1024} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2048} \\\\  & =32\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-280531" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280531" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "32\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A cyclist begins at the position $(2i-j)\\,\\text{m}$ with an initial velocity of $(3i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and an acceleration of $(i+2j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Find the distance from the cyclist to the origin $(|r|)$ after $2$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=2i-j,\\,u=3i+j,\\,a=i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the cyclist after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(2i-j)+(3i+j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+2j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(2i-j)+(6i+2j)+2(i+2j) \\\\  & =(2i-j)+(6i+2j)+(2i+4j) \\\\  & =(10i+5j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the cyclist to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|10i+5j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{125} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-280535" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-280535" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(2i-4j)\\,\\text{m},$ with an acceleration of $(-i+j)\\,{\\text{m/min}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(3i-j)\\,\\text{m/min}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $6$ minutes." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=2i-4j,\\,u=3i-j,\\,a=-i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=6\\,\\text{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(2i-4j)+(3i-j)(6)+\\frac{1}{2}(-i+j)(6)^{2} \\\\  & =(2i-4j)+(18i-6j)+18(-i+j) \\\\  & =(20i-10j)+(-18i+18j) \\\\  & =(2i+8j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|2i+8j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{68} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-136437" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136437" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14\\,\\text{m}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{m}"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{13}\\,\\text{m}"] ["math" "8\\,\\text{m}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{m}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136437" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{m}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves from the origin with a constant velocity of $(3i+j)\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $4$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=3i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(3i+j)(4) \\\\  & =(12i+4j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|12i+4j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{160} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97b1575f788e40a2739abfde575312ac65bcabbd9ec7de9b73ff437e35373c30"} {"question" "q-136436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "6\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{cm}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "q-136436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{cm}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "a696385e8e5970e0eb1520752b215c628ffb85d4b348045c545dc4f267de784b"} {"question" "e-9821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(3\\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{i}) \\: \\textrm{mi}$ with a constant velocity of $(\\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{mi/h}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $2$ hours." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/example-9821.json" "file_sha256" "a2884f8378942210530d39d7cd0ad120094a6501b2051e76565fd92a206d96ad"} {"question" "e-9821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $\\mathbf{u},$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 3\\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{i}, \\qquad \\mathbf u = \\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 2 \\: \\textrm{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(3j-i)+(i-j)(2) \\\\  & =(-i+3j)+(2i-2j) \\\\  & =(i+j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/example-9821.json" "file_sha256" "a2884f8378942210530d39d7cd0ad120094a6501b2051e76565fd92a206d96ad"} {"question" "e-9822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(4\\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j})\\,\\textrm{cm}$ with an acceleration of $(\\mathbf{i} + 3\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{cm/min}^2$ and an initial velocity of $(\\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{cm/min}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $4$ minutes." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/example-9822.json" "file_sha256" "b943d2412939b38e9e1607958847e16639fbdb98ff7cd1e5219957b4f6bcfefd"} {"question" "e-9822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $\\mathbf{a},$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t + \\dfrac12 \\mathbf{a} t^2,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle and $\\mathbf{u}$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 4\\mathbf i - \\mathbf j , \\qquad \\mathbf u = \\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf a = \\mathbf{i} + 3\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 4 \\, \\textrm{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(4i-j)+(i+j)(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+3j)(4)^{2} \\\\  & =(4i-j)+(4i+4j)+8(i+3j) \\\\  & =(8i+3j)+(8i+24j) \\\\  & =(16i+27j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/example-9822.json" "file_sha256" "b943d2412939b38e9e1607958847e16639fbdb98ff7cd1e5219957b4f6bcfefd"} {"question" "e-9824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves from the origin with an acceleration of $(\\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{cm/s}^2$ and an initial velocity of $(-\\mathbf{i}-2\\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{cm/s}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $6$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/example-9824.json" "file_sha256" "a58999a635ea69a847c02eb4b4fe6bbb9b83615d2d06156089bcc30349b40b8d"} {"question" "e-9824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $\\mathbf{a},$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t + \\dfrac12 \\mathbf{a} t^2,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle and $\\mathbf{u}$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 0\\mathbf i +0 \\mathbf j , \\qquad \\mathbf u = -\\mathbf{i}-2\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf a = \\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 6 \\, \\textrm{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(-i-2j)(6)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+j)(6)^{2} \\\\  & =(-6i-12j)+18(i+j) \\\\  & =(-6i-12j)+(18i+18j) \\\\  & =(12i+6j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|12i+6j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{180} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/example-9824.json" "file_sha256" "a58999a635ea69a847c02eb4b4fe6bbb9b83615d2d06156089bcc30349b40b8d"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(9i-64j)\\,\\text{mm}"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/r